"description":"Reference vectors for the phone's live camera-clock fit (Kotlin DeviceClockFit), for porting checks. Each case: feed samples in order to a fresh fit with params {bucket_ms, max_buckets, max_skew_ppm, jump_reset_ms}; every sample is [device_ms_raw, rx_elapsed_ns] where device_ms_raw is the advert's unsigned 32-bit camera time (ms) and rx_elapsed_ns the phone arrival time (ns), all with the case's boot_nonce and timebase_is_master (no resets occur). Algorithm: unwrap device_ms_raw to the candidate raw + k*2^32 nearest the newest sample; offset_ns = rx_elapsed_ns - device_ms*1e6; per bucket floor(device_ms / bucket_ms) keep the minimum offset_ns and its device_ms; keep the newest max_buckets buckets; least-squares line of offset (ms) vs device_ms through the kept minima (centred on the first kept bucket), slope = skew clamped to +-max_skew_ppm; ref_device_ns = (x0 + floor(mean dx)) * 1e6; offset_at_ref_ns = y0 + round((mean dy + skew*(ref - x0 - mean dx)) * 1e6); residual_ms = RMS of the minima about the line (0 with < 3 buckets); with < 2 buckets: ref = that bucket's device_ms, offset = its minimum, skew 0. expected: the fit after the last sample (skew_ppm and residual_ms to 1e-9, the rest exact). conversions: [device_ns, phone_elapsed_ns] = offset_at_ref_ns + device_ns + round(skew*(device_ns - ref_device_ns)), exact.",
"cases":[
